  "intro": "Who buys U.S. pharmaceuticals, **what** they buy and **what they charge** on it. The matrix shows each market's tariff on U.S.-origin goods for the six Chapter 30 product groups, next to the value the U.S. shipped there in 2025; the EU counts as one market because its members share one tariff. Below it, a short profile of each market says whether the U.S. has a trade agreement with it and names the regulator whose approval decides whether the product can be sold at all — for medicines that, not the tariff, is usually the real gate.",
